  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "During their heyday, the prospect of being mugged or otherwise assaulted by Apache gangsters was especially feared by members of the emergent bourgeois. Some of the gangs used a unique type of pistol which was named the \"Apache revolver\" or \"Apache pistol\": a pinfire cartridge pepperbox revolver with no barrel, a set of foldover brass knuckles for a handgrip, and a folding knife mounted right underneath the revolver drum. The Apaches also developed a semi-codified collection of \"tricks\" used in mugging and hand-to-hand combat."
